# Moderation Router Safety

- Do not add broad text catch-all handlers for groups before moderation handlers.
- Any generic `@router.message(F.text)` handlers must be restricted to private chats unless they are part of moderation.
- Keep bot router include order so `moderation_router` can process group text updates.

# Required checks after handler changes

When editing handlers, verify:

1. Group text reaches moderation (`[GUARD TRACE] incoming ... text='...'` appears in bot logs).
2. `verdict` line appears for link text and plain text in group.
3. No new early-return handler swallows group text before moderation.

# Known regression to avoid

Bad pattern:

```python
@router.message(F.text)
async def some_handler(message: Message):
    ...
```

Safe pattern:

```python
@router.message(F.chat.type == "private", F.text)
async def some_handler(message: Message):
    ...
```
